.TH "ROARK\-SIMULATION\-ENVIRONMENT\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-simulation-environment-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-simulation\-environment\-create \- Create an environment
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark simulation environment create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Creates an environment for the project: a noise bed and the level it plays at. Reference it by id when setting a customer flow variant's environment. Roark's curated presets always play at the default level, so this is how a project gets the same bed louder or quieter.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/simulation/environment
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
Display name, shown wherever a flow variant references the environment Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<value>\fR
Optional note on when to use this environment Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-background\-noise\fR \fI<value>\fR
The noise bed played underneath the simulated caller. NONE plays nothing. One of: NONE, AIRPORT, CHILDREN_PLAYING, CITY, COFFEE_SHOP, DRIVING, OFFICE, THUNDERSTORM. Required.
.TP
\fB\-\-background\-noise\-volume\fR \fI<value>\fR
How loud the bed plays, as a gain from 0 (silent) to 1 (as loud as the caller). Defaults to 0.1, which sits well under the caller. Ignored on Vapi endpoints, which have no level control. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
